# ISD — Upstream patches only (`patches/`)

ISD ships **upstream third-party source** (xterm, TinyX, musl, BusyBox, …).
Default: **do not patch** ports to tolerate IR0 kernel gaps.

Complements IR0 `ir0-no-userspace-patches.mdc` and `ir0-userspace-first-linux-abi.mdc`.

## The one exception

The directory **`patches/` at the ISD repo root** is the **only** sanctioned
place for changes to upstream **source trees** when **all** of the following hold:

1. **IR0-first classification** — kernel ABI/uaccess/signal/PTY paths ruled out
   with evidence (`USER_FAULT_FRAME`, `linux-abi-audit`, smokes).
2. **Upstream ownership** — defect is in vendor code (e.g. xterm `button.c`), not
   IR0 kernel or ISD packaging policy alone.
3. **Documentation** — row in `Documentation/PATCHES.md` (symptom, rip, IR0 vs
   Linux repro status, retire criteria).
4. **Tested** — package rebuild + smoke or manual repro showing fix; no “patch
   and hope”.
5. **Upstream candidate** — patch quality suitable for maintainer mailing list
   (xterm → Thomas Dickey); not a permanent fork.

If Linux production reproduces the same crash on the **same upstream version**,
the upstream bug is **unequivocal**. Until then, mark **LINUX PENDING** — still
desconfiar de IR0 first, but do not blame the kernel without proof.

## Forbidden (same spirit as IR0)

| Forbidden | Instead |
|-----------|---------|
| Patch musl/BusyBox/ash for `-EINTR`/TTY/signal ABI | Fix IR0 kernel |
| Patch xterm to hide wrong `TIOCSWINSZ`/PTY behavior | Fix IR0 devfs/PTY |
| Ad-hoc edits in `packages/*/src` without a patch file | Add `patches/<pkg>/NNNN-….patch` + doc |
| “Works in QEMU” without rebuild + smoke | `make build` + profile smoke |

## Layout and wiring

```text
patches/<package>/*.patch     ← canonical new patches
packages/<pkg>/patches/       ← legacy; avoid new files here
scripts/apply-isd-patches.sh  ← applies both; idempotent
```

Applied on `make fetch` and before X autotools builds.

## Agent checklist (before adding a patch)

- [ ] IR0 kernel fix attempted or ruled out with log/symbol evidence
- [ ] Component identified (xterm client vs X server vs kernel)
- [ ] `Documentation/PATCHES.md` updated
- [ ] Patch applies with `-p1` on clean upstream tarball
- [ ] Package rebuild PASS
- [ ] Smoke or manual repro PASS
- [ ] Linux repro status recorded (done / pending / N/A with reason)
- [ ] Upstream submission path noted

## Anti-patterns

- Expanding `patches/` for every ISD convenience tweak.
- Duplicating IR0 `ir0-patches` belts in ISD.
- Marking “upstream bug” without `addr2line`/backtrace on **vendor** symbols.
- Leaving stale patches after upstream merge (retire per `Documentation/PATCHES.md`).
